Subject: vmwarefusion: create the VM with suspend disabled

Every Container Tools VM that has run in production had suspend.disabled = "TRUE": it came from
Wowfunhappy's patched docker-machine (his recipe: "disables suspend in vmware because that screws
up stuff"), and docker-machine-migrate kept it. Stock 0.16.2 doesn't write it, so a VM our .pkg
created ran in an untested configuration. Write it at create, as his did (2026-11-24); payload's
disable_suspend adds it to a VM created before this.

--- a/drivers/vmwarefusion/vmx_darwin.go
+++ b/drivers/vmwarefusion/vmx_darwin.go
@@ -69,4 +69,5 @@
 numvcpus = "{{.CPU}}"
 hgfs.mapRootShare = "FALSE"
 hgfs.linkRootShare = "FALSE"
+suspend.disabled = "TRUE"
 `
